stepconf generator tests
=========================

Non-GUI tests for the stepconf configuration wizard.

stepconf is a GTK application, but its config-emitting code lives in modules
that import only the Python standard library (build_HAL.py imports os/time/
shutil, build_INI.py adds sys/importlib).  Those modules can therefore be
exercised directly -- without a display or the linuxcnc runtime -- by
constructing the generator class with small stand-ins for the wizard's data
and private-data objects and asserting on the HAL/INI text it writes.

This is useful because the wizards otherwise have no automated coverage: the
CI test run is headless (runtests unsets DISPLAY), so nothing exercises
stepconf or pncconf, and generator regressions ship undetected.

  parport2-doublestep-reset/  - a step signal on the 2nd parallel port gets its
                                doublestep reset emitted on parport.0 instead of
                                parport.1 (build_HAL.py connect_output).
